  question: 'Can a Backyard Building Improve Property Value?',
  answer: [
    'It may improve usefulness, marketability, buyer confidence and long-term appeal, but no honest builder can guarantee a specific resale return or appraisal result.',
    'The real impact depends on the property, neighborhood, market, construction quality, approved use, placement, visual fit, maintenance and how clearly a future buyer understands the building’s purpose.',
    'A workshop that solves a real storage problem, an office that supports daily work or a garden building that organizes outdoor living can create meaningful value even when no future sale price can be predicted.',
  ],
  sections: [
    {
      type: 'cards', id: 'types', eyebrow: 'Understanding Value', title: 'A Building Can Create Several Kinds of Value at Once', nav: 'Types of Value',
      items: [
        { title: 'Functional value', text: 'It solves a practical problem: storage, workshop, gardening, hobbies, work from home or pool support.' },
        { title: 'Lifestyle value', text: 'Space that makes daily life easier or more enjoyable without adding onto the house.' },
        { title: 'Visual value', text: 'Good proportions, roofline, siding, trim and placement make the yard feel complete.' },
        { title: 'Marketability', text: 'A useful, attractive, easy-to-understand improvement gives future buyers another reason to like the property.' },
        { title: 'Buyer confidence', text: 'Quality construction, proper approvals, records and maintenance reduce uncertainty.' },
        { title: 'Long-term flexibility', text: 'A well-designed building can shift from storage to hobbies, work or gardening as needs change.' },
      ],
    },
    {
      type: 'cards', id: 'strengthen', title: 'The Building Should Look Planned, Useful and Right for the Property', nav: 'What Strengthens Value',
      items: [
        { title: 'Clear purpose', list: ['Workshop', 'Backyard office', 'Garden building', 'Studio', 'Pool-support building', 'Organized storage'] },
        { title: 'Property fit', list: ['Appropriate size', 'Compatible roof form', 'Coordinated siding and trim', 'Thoughtful placement', 'Useful paths', 'Landscape integration'] },
        { title: 'Construction quality', list: ['Stable foundation', 'Durable floor', 'Sound framing', 'Proper roof construction', 'Weather-resistant exterior', 'Maintainable details'] },
      ],
      note: 'Usefulness comes before a resale promise. The building should first improve the property for the homeowner paying for it. If it later supports stronger marketability, that is a bonus, not a guarantee.',
    },
    {
      type: 'cards', id: 'red-flags', title: 'Conditions That Weaken the Building’s Value Story', nav: 'Value Red Flags',
      items: [
        { title: 'Guaranteed-return claims', text: 'Be cautious of anyone promising a specific increase in selling price.' },
        { title: 'Unclear permits or approvals', text: 'Unresolved zoning, setback, HOA or easement questions create later uncertainty.' },
        { title: 'Overstated legal use', text: 'A finished building is not a legal bedroom, dwelling or rental unless it qualifies.' },
        { title: 'Poor property fit', text: 'Oversized or awkwardly placed buildings feel like obstructions.' },
        { title: 'Temporary appearance', text: 'Weak foundations, poor trim or roof problems make even a new building feel disposable.' },
        { title: 'Deferred maintenance', text: 'Neglected roofing, paint, caulk, drainage or doors erode buyer confidence quickly.' },
      ],
    },
    {
      type: 'table', id: 'hype', dark: true, title: 'Trustworthy Guidance Avoids Promises No Builder Can Control', nav: 'Value vs. Sales Hype',
      head: ['Weak claim', 'Better planning language', 'Why it matters'],
      rows: [
        ['“This will increase your property value.”', 'A well-planned building may improve usefulness, marketability and buyer confidence.', 'Markets and appraisals can’t be guaranteed'],
        ['“You will get your money back.”', 'Judge it by current usefulness, enjoyment, quality, fit and possible appeal.', 'General examples can’t predict one property'],
        ['“Any shed adds value.”', 'Impact varies with quality, placement, purpose, appearance and upkeep.', 'A poorly planned building can hurt presentation'],
