      ],
      note: 'Home types, lot sizes and buyer expectations vary widely across Greater Cincinnati, Northern Kentucky and Southeast Indiana. A building that fits one suburban lot may dominate another, so confirm the project suits your exact property before assuming any financial benefit.',
    },
  ],
  disclaimer: 'This guide is general planning education, not real estate, appraisal, tax or financial advice. No builder can guarantee how a future buyer, market, appraiser, lender, insurer or taxing authority will treat a backyard building.',
  faqs: [
    { q: 'Will a backyard building automatically increase my home value?', a: 'No. The impact depends on quality, usefulness, placement, condition, approvals, the market and whether future buyers see it as a benefit.' },
    { q: 'Why say “value impact” instead of promising a return?', a: 'It recognizes real benefits, like usefulness, organization, appeal and buyer confidence, without pretending anyone can predict a future appraisal or sale price.' },
    { q: 'Can a finished backyard building be marketed as living space?', a: 'Not automatically. That depends on property-specific zoning, building code, permits, utilities and occupancy rules.' },
    { q: 'Does building on site help the value story?', a: 'It can. On-site building supports property-specific placement, foundation planning, roof proportions and exterior coordination, which help the building look intentionally integrated.' },
    { q: 'Should I design for myself or a future buyer?', a: 'Start with a real use that benefits your household now, but avoid choices so specialized that someone else couldn’t understand the building.' },
  ],
  related: ['07', '17', '18', '16'],
  pages: [['Buildings & Pricing', 'Every model, size and siding with published prices.', '/buildings/']],
  ctaTitle: 'Choose the Building Around the Use, the Property and the Long-Term Plan',
  ctaText: 'Define how the building will be used, confirm it fits the property, understand approvals and site conditions, and choose durable, maintainable construction. Handled well, those fundamentals give the building its best chance to add lasting value.',
};
---
<GuidePage page={page} />
